        "title": "fix(agent): check updateSessionEntry return value for pendingFinalDelivery write",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where `pendingFinalDelivery` state written via `updateSessionEntry` silently discards write failures. If the store write fails (IO error, disk full, permission denied), the delivery state is lost and restart recovery reads stale state — the reply is never re-sent.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nAdded `requireWriteSuccess: true` to the `updateSessionEntry` options for the `pendingFinalDelivery` write. This is a durable state write where silent failure would cause data loss. The `requireWriteSuccess` option makes the store throw on write failure instead of silently recovering, so the caller (`runReplyAgent`) properly fails when this critical metadata cannot be persisted. This is the same pattern used in 4 other call sites for critical state writes: `dashboard-session-title.ts:109`, `session-lifecycle-state.ts:285`, `main-session-restart-recovery.ts:217`, `state-migrations.ts:5693`.\n\n## User Impact\n\nNone in normal operation. On store write failure, the agent run now throws instead of silently losing pending delivery state.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- **Real environment tested**: Linux, Node 22, branch `fix/check-pending-delivery-write`\n\n- **3-tier failure-injection proof** (`pending-final-delivery.store-write-failure.test.ts`):\n\n  **Test 1** — Exact PR code path: mocks `writeTextAtomic` to throw ENOENT and verifies `updateSessionEntry` with `requireWriteSuccess: true` propagates the error.\n  **Test 2** — Full write path with `requireWriteSuccess: true`: mocks `replaceFileAtomic` (one level deeper, at the `@openclaw/fs-safe` boundary) and verifies ENOENT propagates.\n  **Test 3** — Full write path WITHOUT `requireWriteSuccess`: same ENOENT mock but the store silently swallows the error — proving current `main` silently loses data.\n\n  ```console\n  $ pnpm exec vitest run src/auto-reply/reply/pending-final-delivery.store-write-failure.test.ts --config test/vitest/vitest.auto-reply.config.ts --reporter=verbose\n\n   ✓ |auto-reply| pending-final-delivery.store-write-failure.test.ts >\n       pendingFinalDelivery requireWriteSuccess >\n       propagates store write failure WITH requireWriteSuccess:true (PR #102128)\n   ✓ |auto-reply| pending-final-delivery.store-write-failure.test.ts >\n       pendingFinalDelivery requireWriteSuccess >\n       full path: ENOENT propagates WITH requireWriteSuccess:true\n   ✓ |auto-reply| pending-final-delivery.store-write-failure.test.ts >\n       pendingFinalDelivery requireWriteSuccess >\n       full path: ENOENT silently swallowed WITHOUT requireWriteSuccess (current main)\n\n   Test Files  1 passed (1)\n        Tests  3 passed (3)\n  ```\n\n  Test details:\n\n  1. Creates a real session store on disk, injects ENOENT at `writeTextAtomic`, calls `updateSessionEntry` with the same arguments as the `pendingFinalDelivery` path, asserts the error propagates.\n  2. Creates a store, injects ENOENT at `replaceFileAtomic` (lower-level atomic write), calls `saveSessionStore` with `requireWriteSuccess: true`, asserts the error throws through the retry-exhausted ENOENT handler (`store.ts:994-997`).\n  3. Same setup but WITHOUT `requireWriteSuccess` — the call resolves silently (`store.ts:998-999`), demonstrating the current `main` data-loss behavior.\n\n- **Store contract proof**: The `requireWriteSuccess` flag controls ENOENT behavior at two distinct store paths:\n  - **Windows retry loop** (`store.ts:944-948`): Without the flag, ENOENT on the first retry is silently swallowed; with it, the error is thrown.\n  - **Non-Windows full write path** (`store.ts:994-999`): Without the flag, repeated ENOENT is silently recovered; with it, the error is thrown.\n\n- **Existing tests**:\n\n  ```console\n  $ node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/auto-reply/reply/pending-final-delivery.test.ts\n  Test Files  1 passed (1)\n       Tests  4 passed (4)\n  ```\n\n## Regression Test Plan\n\n```console\nnode scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/auto-reply/reply/pending-final-delivery.test.ts\nnode scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/auto-reply/reply/pending-final-delivery.store-write-failure.test.ts\n```\n\n---\n\nAI-assisted.",
